    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d85">

                <pb facs="0279" n="209" xml:id="pg209"/>

                <head>No. 85.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Young to Mr.
                    Frelinghuysen.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-08-30"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 30, 1883</date>.
                        (Received October 20.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 244.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose certain
                    correspondence with the consul at Canton in reference to a recent disturbance in
                    that city arising: out of the folly of some Europeans, which unhappily led to
                    loss of life.</p>
                <p>The Department will not fail to note the forbearance shown by the Chinese
                    authorities, and the promptitude with which the viceroy intervened to preserve
                    order and secure the interests and safety of the foreign settlement.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JNO. RUSSELL YOUNG.</signed></closer>





